ever, with three clubs on the board, any club in their hand makes a flush that beats my weak two pair (Aces and Sevens). Given that I'm already ahead +21,100 chips cumulatively in the match with only 4 hands remaining, the optimal strategy is to check and see the showdown for free rather than risk chips on a marginal hand. If opponent had a strong hand, they likely would have bet at some point.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
