e to **check (0)**. The opponent showed weakness by checking after their pre-flop aggression. With 12 outs (~48% to improve), I have good equity. Checking allows me to see the turn for free while maintaining pot control. If I hit my flush or Ace on the turn, I can then extract value. If I miss, I can reassess based on opponent's turn action. Given my overall chip lead in the match (24,400 cumulative), preserving chips and avoiding unnecessary risk on a drawing hand is prudent.\n\n# Answer: 0"}
